/*
 * Fallback bindings for web-only builds (browser shell without Tauri).
 *
 * The real `src/bindings.ts` is generated by tauri-specta on Rust builds and
 * is gitignored — a fresh checkout (CI, a web-only clone) has no such file,
 * and `vite build` fails resolving `../bindings`. Whenever the generated
 * file is absent, web builds copy THIS file over it (see
 * .github/workflows/deploy-web.yml and build-preview-web.bat):
 *
 *   if [ ! -f src/bindings.ts ]; then cp src/bindings-fallback.ts src/bindings.ts; fi
 *
 * It mirrors the runtime section of the dev shim (rejecting commands, no-op
 * event listeners, session/funding bridges to the active source) with all
 * specta types aliased to `any`, so both `vite build` and `tsc --noEmit`
 * pass against it. Real Tauri builds overwrite it with the specta export.
 * Keep the runtime behavior in sync with src/bindings.ts by eye.
 */

